From dd4b512b4613a602164eea163fc6183578d8f4ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wb <wb@local>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:40:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rtl819x kernel: dma cache exports for GPL out-of-tree driver

The non-coherent-MIPS cache-op trio _dma_cache_wback_inv / _dma_cache_wback /
_dma_cache_inv is defined in arch/mips/mm/cache.c (under
CONFIG_DMA_NONCOHERENT, assigned by c-r4k.c) but is not exported for
modules, so the GPL rtl8192cd radio driver fails at modpost with
"undefined" symbols. Export them exactly like the stock Realtek SDK
kernel did.

---
 .../030-mips-rtl819x-dma-exports.patch        | 29 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 target/linux/rtl819x/patches-6.18/030-mips-rtl819x-dma-exports.patch

diff --git a/target/linux/rtl819x/patches-6.18/030-mips-rtl819x-dma-exports.patch b/target/linux/rtl819x/patches-6.18/030-mips-rtl819x-dma-exports.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1ba1515
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/rtl819x/patches-6.18/030-mips-rtl819x-dma-exports.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+From: OpenWrt RTL819x bring-up <noreply@example.invalid>
+Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: rtl819x: export legacy non-coherent DMA cache ops
+ for out-of-tree drivers
+
+The non-coherent-MIPS cache-op trio _dma_cache_wback_inv /
+_dma_cache_wback / _dma_cache_inv is defined in arch/mips/mm/cache.c
+(under CONFIG_DMA_NONCOHERENT, assigned by c-r4k.c) but is no longer
+exported for modules, so GPL out-of-tree platform drivers that use the
+vendor cache-maintenance API (rtl8192cd radio driver) fail at modpost
+with "undefined" symbols. Export them exactly like the stock Realtek
+SDK kernel did.
+
+---
+--- a/arch/mips/mm/cache.c
++++ b/arch/mips/mm/cache.c
+@@ -80,6 +80,13 @@ void (*_dma_cache_wback_inv)(unsigned long start, unsigned long size);
+void (*_dma_cache_wback)(unsigned long start, unsigned long size);
+void (*_dma_cache_inv)(unsigned long start, unsigned long size);
+
++/* Exported for GPL out-of-tree platform drivers (e.g. the Realtek
++ * rtl8192cd radio driver) that perform manual cache maintenance on this
++ * non-coherent MIPS SoC, like the stock vendor SDK kernel does. */
++EXPORT_SYMBOL(_dma_cache_wback_inv);
++EXPORT_SYMBOL(_dma_cache_wback);
++EXPORT_SYMBOL(_dma_cache_inv);
++
+#endif /* CONFIG_DMA_NONCOHERENT */
+
+/*
-- 
